{{!
    @template local_coursegen/template_space_row

    One virtual space row: a place in a section where the professor must (or
    may) provide an activity of their own when creating a course from this
    template. The same markup template_space_rows.js renders client-side when
    a new space is added, so a freshly added row is never anything but this
    same markup either way.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-for="spacerow" data-space-id data-modname data-required on the row,
      read back by collectSpacesForSection() (the save payload).
    * data-region="space-instruction" on the instruction subtitle.
    * data-region="space-badge" on the clickable badge (reopens the settings).
    * data-region="space-edit" / "space-remove" on the row's two icons.

    Context variables:
    * spaceid string        - Unique within the page (a saved id, or a
                              client-only "new-N" one for an unsaved space).
    * name string           - The activity type's display name.
    * typelabel string      - The same, for the Type column.
    * modname string        - The activity type's module name (e.g. "resource").
    * icon string           - The type's icon, as the markup Moodle's own activity chooser
                              returns for it (an image tag); printed unescaped on purpose.
    * requiredvalue int     - 1 when required, 0 when optional.
    * badge string          - "Space · Required" / "Space · Optional".
    * instruction string    - What the professor has to provide; may be empty.
    * hasinstruction bool   - Whether instruction is not empty.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "spaceid": "new-1",
        "name": "File",
        "typelabel": "File",
        "modname": "resource",
        "icon": "<img src='https://example.com/resource.svg' class='icon activityicon' alt=''>",
        "requiredvalue": 1,
        "badge": "Space · Required",
        "instruction": "Upload the weekly guide as a PDF.",
        "hasinstruction": true
    }
}}
<tr class="tpl-row-space" data-for="spacerow" data-space-id="{{spaceid}}"
    data-modname="{{modname}}" data-required="{{requiredvalue}}">
    <td class="align-middle tpl-select-col"></td>
    <td class="align-middle">
        {{! The icon is markup built by Moodle core for the chooser (core_course_get_course_content_items), which core itself prints with triple braces. }}
        <span class="mr-2">{{{icon}}}</span><span>{{name}}</span>
        <button type="button" class="tpl-badge tpl-badge-space tpl-space-tag ml-2" data-region="space-badge"
                title="{{#str}} template_space_edit, local_coursegen {{/str}}">{{badge}}</button>
        <div class="tpl-space-instruction text-muted small{{^hasinstruction}} d-none{{/hasinstruction}}"
             data-region="space-instruction">{{instruction}}</div>
    </td>
    <td class="align-middle text-muted">{{typelabel}}</td>
    <td class="align-middle text-right">
        <div class="tpl-instance-actions">
            <button type="button" class="tpl-instance-icon-btn" data-region="space-edit"
                    title="{{#str}} template_space_edit, local_coursegen {{/str}}">
                {{#pix}} t/edit, core {{/pix}}
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="tpl-instance-icon-btn tpl-instance-icon-danger" data-region="space-remove"
                    title="{{#str}} template_space_remove, local_coursegen {{/str}}">
                {{#pix}} t/delete, core {{/pix}}
            </button>
        </div>
    </td>
</tr>
